-- title:
--   Box sheet as fundamental domain for Z(K)N(K)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, and work with the Borel measurable structures on $\mathbb{A}_K$ and on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$. Inside $H :=$ `rationalCentreUnipotent K`, the subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ generated by the image of $K^\times$ under $a \mapsto \mathrm{scalar}(a)$ composed with the diagonal embedding $K \to \mathbb{A}_K$ together with the group of adelic unipotents $n(u) = \begin{pmatrix}1&u\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, $u \in \mathbb{A}_K$, put $P :=$ the join of that rational centre with the range of $x \mapsto n(x)$ for $x \in K$ pushed into $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, and let $T \subseteq H$ be the image of the adelic box $\{x : x_\infty \in \mathrm{infiniteBox}\ K,\ x_{\mathrm{fin}} \in \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_K\}$ under $u \mapsto n(u)$. The measure on $H$ is `rationalCentreUnipotentHaar K`, the sum over $a \in K^\times$ of the translates by $\mathrm{scalar}(a)$ of the pushforward along $u \mapsto n(u)$ of $(\mu(\mathrm{adelicBox}\ K))^{-1}\mu$, where $\mu$ is the additive Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_K$. The assertion is fivefold: $P \le H$; $P$ is countable; $T$ is measurable; $T$ is a fundamental domain for the action of $P$, viewed as a subgroup of $H$, on $H$ for that measure; and for every measurable $F : H \to [0,\infty]$ one has $\int_T F \, d(\text{that measure}) = \int_{\mathrm{adelicBox}\,K} F(n(u)) \, d\big((\mu(\mathrm{adelicBox}\,K))^{-1}\mu\big)(u)$.
--
--   This is the fundamental-domain and unfolding statement for the discrete subgroup $Z(K)N(K)$ inside $Z(K)N(\mathbb{A}_K)$, with the sheet of unipotents over a fundamental box for $K \subset \mathbb{A}_K$ as fundamental domain, normalised so that it has total mass one. It is used in the Rankin–Selberg unfolding on $\mathrm{GL}_2$, being cited by the lemmas that convert integrals over $Z(K)N(K)\backslash \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ into integrals involving Whittaker coefficients over $K \backslash \mathbb{A}_K$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_isFundamentalDomain_boxSheet_rationalCentreUnipotent.lean

